<title>JAPAN: DKB ask-only on TSE after four officials' arrest.</title>
<headline>DKB ask-only on TSE after four officials' arrest.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank Ltd (DKB) was ask-only on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on Friday morning after the arrest of four of its officials on Thursday on suspicion of violating the Commercial Code.</p>
<p>By 0011 GMT, DKB shares were ask-only at 1,310 yen against Thursday's close of 1,330.  </p>
<p>Later in the morning, DKB shares were traded at 1,290 yen by 0027 GMT.</p>
<p>Prosecutors on Thursday arrested four DKB officials on suspicion of making illegal loans worth 11.78 billion yen to a racketeer.</p>
</text>
